* Fender '65 Twin Reverb reissue vibrato (optical tremolo), drawing 037627 rev E: V5A is a three-section
* RC phase-shift oscillator (speed pot in the first section), V5B a pulse driver whose plate current
* lights the LED of the optocoupler OP1 through R62. The photocell side (OP1 pins 3/4) is part of
* preamp.net: it shunts the mixing node through the Intensity pot, and the engine sets its resistance
* from the LED current. This circuit is solved at a low rate of its own (see "vibrato" in amp.json).
*
* The footswitch / Vibrato-off state is the bias reference node t31: -8.5 V (V5A cut off) when off,
* about -0.35 V when the footswitch brings it to ground through ~10k. C38 (220p) is left out: its
* time constant is far below the low solve rate.

V VRAIL x 100 393

* V5A oscillator.
R R54 x p5a 220k
T V5A n3 p5a k5a ECC83
R R60 k5a 0 2k7
C C27 k5a 0 22u
C C24 p5a n1 22n
C C25 n1 n2 10n
C C26 n2 n3 10n
R R55 n1 ns 91k
R R_SPEED ns 0 1.5M
R R57 n2 t31 1M
R R58 n3 t31 1M

* Bias reference: -65 V behind 10k + 1.8M, 270k to ground, 10u; the footswitch shorts it to ground.
V VBIAS bs 10k -65
R R59 bs t31 1.8M
R R76 t31 0 270k
C C37 t31 0 10u
R SW_VIB t31 0 1e12

* V5B driver and the LED: 100k from the rail, the LED (pins 2 -> 1) in series with the plate, 10M across.
T V5B n2 p5b k5b ECC83
R R61 k5b 0 100k
C C28 k5b 0 22u
R R62 x ln 100k
D LED ln p5b SIGNAL
R R63 ln p5b 10M
C C40 p5b 0 22n
